  "configuration_id": "config_037",
  "reason": "The current best is config_039 (multimodal, multiprofile, scVI_n200, ViT-L, transformer, weighted) at 0.7250. All major design axes (RNA encoder, profile, image encoder, fusion) are well-supported by evidence: scVI_n200 > PCA > scGPT, multiprofile >> single-profile, ViT-L > ResNet50, weighted > concat. The one remaining untested degree of freedom in this top-performing setup is aggregation: in RNA-only multiprofile, transformer (0.6530) edged out avgpool (0.6501) by a small margin (~0.003). Config_037 (same as config_039 but with avgpool instead of transformer) isolates whether that small aggregation preference holds in the multimodal ViT-L context. As the final experiment, this is the most logical exploitation step: it directly probes the closest untested variant of the best configuration, and if avgpool performs comparably or (unlikely) better, it would either confirm the robustness of the current best or reveal a new top result. No other untested config combines all the empirically superior choices, making this the highest-value last test."
}

